# LADE — ignored paths.
#
# A role home is a REAL directory at ~/.hermes/profiles/<role> whose content
# entries are symlinked from this repository, so Hermes creates its runtime state
# (state.db, memories, sessions, cache, logs, backups, locks, gateway and plugin
# metadata, and — on first run — a copy of its bundled skills) in the home, outside
# git. These rules are the second line of defence: they keep stray runtime state in
# profiles/<role>/ out of a commit while `make verify` reports it as
# `runtime_state_in_repo`. The layout itself is guarded by
# scripts/repair_profile_homes.sh --check.
#
# Kept in git under profiles/<role>/: AGENTS.md, SOUL.md, profile.yaml,
# config.yaml. The skills/ directory is generated by setup.sh from the role
# manifest and is ignored: the manifest is the source of truth.

# Everything under profiles/<role>/, then the four source files back in.
profiles/*/*
!profiles/*/AGENTS.md
!profiles/*/SOUL.md
!profiles/*/profile.yaml
!profiles/*/config.yaml

# Local tooling
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.DS_Store
# Makefile: local archives and compiled helpers
.lade-backups/

# Task instances and artifacts are produced at run time, never committed here.
task.md
